omp-target-region-slot-reuse.m on the machine's GPU, at -O0 and -O2: the
region's slot, used by 600 regions one after another, is cleared by each
region's device as it starts, and their chunks, which the host keeps, hold
no earlier region's tables. Every chunk is back with the host at the end.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -fopenmp -fdo-loops --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/omp-target-region-slot-reuse.m -o %t0
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 120 %t0 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/omp-target-region-slot-reuse.m -o %t2
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 120 %t2 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
CHECK:300 of 300 rounds were right
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated
